  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\nSkies are mostly clear this morning. Surface pressure gradients\nare trending stronger offshore, currently around -9.4 mb SAN-TPH\nand -3.3 mb SAN-DAG. Breezy northeast winds gusting 25-35 mph\ncontinue below the passes and canyons and on the coastal mountain\nslopes. Winds will strengthen slightly through the morning with\nisolated gusts to 45 mph, then weaken during the afternoon and\nevening. Winds turn more easterly on Sunday with breezy conditions\ncontinuing along the San Diego and Riverside County coastal\nmountain slopes and passes. Warming trend continues into Sunday\nwhen highs will be anywhere from 5-15 degrees above normal, with\nthe greatest departure from normal in the coastal areas. Highs\nwill generally be in the mid 80s to around 90 for the coastal\nareas and valleys, 60s to low 70s in the mountains, low to mid 70s\nin the high desert, and mid 80s in the low desert.\n\nThe upper level ridge weakens Monday and Tuesday with much weaker\noffshore flow, allowing for a couple degrees of cooling each day\nand otherwise benign weather. An upper level ridge amplifies\nacross the Southwest on Wednesday ahead of a digging trough off\nthe West Coast, bringing minor warming. \n\nSolutions diverge around Thursday as about 58% of the global\nensemble members maintain upper level ridging and warm/dry weather\nin Southern California, while 19% have a trough far enough south\nalong the coast for some light precipitation and much cooler\nweather, and the remaining 21% with a less amplified trough for \nless cooling but still dry weather. As we head into Friday, there\nis better agreement for weak troughing over So Cal for more\ncooling and a 15% chance of light precipitation. Saturday becomes\nquestionable again as ensemble members differ on the evolution of\nthe short wave in the southern stream of the jet, which will\ndictate how much if any additional precipitation occurs, though\nthe general consensus shows at least light precipitation (20-30%\nchance). High confidence that any Atmospheric Rivers will remain \nto the north late next week, so chances of at least moderate\nprecipitation (0.50\" or more) is 20% or less for the mountains\nwestward.",
